Qt 5.15 already specializes std::hash for QString/QStringRef/QByteArray/QBitArray
(src/corelib/tools/qhashfunctions.h, lines 204-209) with no disableable guard, so
kdevelop-pg-qt's own q_Hash_to_tr1_hash(QBitArray) becomes a redefinition:

    kdev-pg/kdev-pg-regexp.cpp:54:1: error: redefinition of 'hash<QBitArray>'
    .../qhashfunctions.h:209:1: note: previous definition is here

Guard the local definition for Qt < 5.15 only. Zero functional change on 5.15,
where Qt's own specialization is used (same qHash-based implementation).

--- a/kdev-pg/kdev-pg-regexp.cpp
+++ b/kdev-pg/kdev-pg-regexp.cpp
@@ -51,7 +51,9 @@
     };                                                      \
 }
 
+#if QT_VERSION < QT_VERSION_CHECK(5, 15, 0)
 q_Hash_to_tr1_hash(QBitArray)
+#endif
 
 namespace KDevPG
 {
